  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Systems Planning and Analysis obligated $339M in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. Systems Planning and Analysis received 66 awards so far, with an average award size of $5.1M. Systems Planning and Analysis obligations are down 7.8% year over year. Systems Planning and Analysis saw larger obligations from earlier fiscal years: FY21 $132M, FY22 $167M, FY23 $208M, FY24 $260M, and FY25 $368M. Systems Planning and Analysis sold primarily Engineering Services with obligations of $230M, followed by All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $61.3M, Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) at $24M, Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services at $22.6M, Building Inspection Services at $803K, and Software Publishers at $95.8K. Systems Planning and Analysis received most of its obligations from the Department of Defense at $318M, with smaller amounts from the Department of Homeland Security at $16.7M and the Department of Energy at $4M. Current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did obligations change year over year?",
        "body": "Systems Planning and Analysis obligations are down 7.8% year over year. Systems Planning and Analysis obligated $339M in FY2026 to date compared with $368M in FY25. Systems Planning and Analysis had a multi-year rise in obligations from FY21 through FY25 before the FY26 decline."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the main buyers and what does the company sell?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the main buyer, obligating $318M. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $16.7M and the Department of Energy obligated $4M. Engineering Services is the largest market at $230M, with other significant markets including All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $61.3M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) at $24M."
      }
